CM ============================================================
CM  TM-SC-NEC-005: Screwdriver Antenna — 20m Band
CM  2.4m whip, base loading coil, 4 horizontal elevated radials
CM  Frequency: 14.000–14.350 MHz (8 points, 0.050 MHz step)
CM
CM  Loading coil (series RL at base, segment 1 of GW1):
CM    R = 1.171 ohm  (Rcoil = Xant / Q, Q~320)
CM    X = 374.8 ohm  (XL required to resonate 2.4m whip on 20m)
CM
CM  Whip: 2.4m, avg radius 0.006m, 20 segments
CM  Radials: 4 x 2.4m at z=0.005m, 90 deg spacing
CM  Ground: real (Sommerfeld-Norton), eps=13, sigma=0.005
CM  Feed: 1V voltage source at GW1, seg 1
CM
CM  Tuning note: 20m is the primary DX band for HF mobile.
CM  Quarter-wave at 14 MHz = 5.36m; whip is 2.4m = 44.8% of QW.
CM  Significant loading required. Efficiency still acceptable for
CM  mobile work. Radiation resistance ~15 ohm typical for this
CM  loading configuration. Pattern peaks at ~25-30 deg elevation.
